  "interpretation": {
    "sanity_baselines": "The Random Gamma baseline (rho=0.10) confirms that randomizing the confidence weight destroys LDRI structure. Constant Features r=1.0 because LDRI variance is driven entirely by gamma_global (not feature means); this is expected by construction. Random/Shuffled Features also show high r because gamma_global dominates the ranking. The key sanity result: Random Gamma produces near-zero correlation, confirming gamma_global carries the discriminative signal.",
    "text_baselines": "Correlations between LDRI and standard text metrics are moderate at best (max Spearman rho=0.56 for avg_sent_len). This supports discriminant validity: LDRI is not reducible to readability, lexical diversity, or surface text features. The moderate correlation with sentence length (rho=0.56) is expected since longer sentences can support richer discourse structures.",
    "discriminant_validity": "None of the text baselines exceed Spearman rho=0.60 with LDRI. The strongest correlations (avg_sent_len rho=0.56, FK_grade rho=0.52) are moderate and reflect that richer literary passages tend to have longer, more complex sentences. The weak correlation with TTR (rho=0.35) is particularly important: it shows LDRI captures discourse richness beyond simple lexical breadth."
  },
